337	135,1440,425,1918	337. Flower of No. 2.	A Pale Jewel-weed flower hanging from its slender stalk: the large dotted sac curving back into a little hooked spur, with the lobed petals spread at its mouth.
338	485,1380,1000,1920	338. Calyx and corolla displayed.	The six pieces of the flower pulled apart and laid out: a rounded upper piece, two small side sepals, the two unequally two-lobed inner petals, and the large spurred sac below.
